A rectangular gate is $1.6\text{ m}$ wide and $1.2\text{ m}$ high. Find the length $d$ of its diagonal brace.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,3);
\draw (0,0)--(4,3);
\path (2,0) node[below] {$1.6\text{ m}$} (4,1.5) node[right] {$1.2\text{ m}$} (2,1.5) node[above left] {$d$};
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A $6\text{ m}$ ladder leans against a vertical wall. Its foot is $2\text{ m}$ from the wall on level ground. How high does it reach? Round to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(2,0)--(0,4)--cycle;
\draw (0.25,0)--(0.25,0.25)--(0,0.25);
\path (1,0) node[below] {$2\text{ m}$} (0,2) node[left] {$h$} (1,2) node[above right] {$6\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two vertical posts are $3.5\text{ m}$ and $5.9\text{ m}$ tall and stand $7\text{ m}$ apart on level ground. Find the length $s$ of a straight string joining their tops. Round to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-0.3,0)--(4.3,0);
\draw (0,0)--(0,2);
\draw (4,0)--(4,3.37);
\draw (0,2)--(4,3.37);
\draw[dashed] (0,2)--(4,2);
\draw (3.75,2)--(3.75,2.25)--(4,2.25);
\path (0,1) node[left] {$3.5\text{ m}$} (4,1.685) node[right] {$5.9\text{ m}$} (2,0) node[below] {$7\text{ m}$} (2,2.685) node[above] {$s$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The vertical side of the right-angled triangle is the difference in the post heights.
$5.9-3.5=2.4\text{ m}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(4,0)--(4,1.37);
\draw (0,0)--(4,1.37);
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\path (2,0) node[below] {$7\text{ m}$} (4,0.685) node[right] {$2.4\text{ m}$} (2,0.685) node[above] {$s$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}s&=\sqrt{7^{2}+2.4^{2}}\\&=\sqrt{54.76}\\&=7.4\text{ m}\end{aligned}$

