Find the perpendicular height $h$ of an equilateral triangle with side length $14\text{ cm}$. Give your answer in exact surd form.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(4,0)--(2,3.464)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (2,3.464)--(2,0);
\draw (2,0.25)--(2.25,0.25)--(2.25,0);
\path (1,1.732) node[above left] {$14\text{ cm}$} (3,1.732) node[above right] {$14\text{ cm}$} (2,0) node[below] {$14\text{ cm}$} (2,1.7) node[right] {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rectangle has diagonal $12\text{ cm}$ and is twice as long as it is wide. Find its dimensions to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,2);
\draw (0,0)--(4,2);
\draw (3.75,0)--(3.75,0.25)--(4,0.25);
\path (2,1) node[above left] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
